        {
          "id": 1615650897,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I think I wanted to replace the whole complicated `ssl_create_decoder` -> `ssl_cipher_init` chain with something simpler for TLS 1.3. The `SslDecoder` struct is doing a lot of things combined. The function (and the `tls13_cipher` struct type) was added for QUIC, with a refactoring in the TLS dissector in mind, but that never happened.\n\nGiven that it is unused, it's probably okay to remove it. I don't see a refactor happening any time soon unless someone else has time for it :)",
          "author": {
            "id": 2415432,
            "username": "Lekensteyn",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Peter Wu",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/efcf30db53f30b15e7c905ef37bd4dc44d87573bd92baf97cd707115d3fcd0c0?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/Lekensteyn"
          },
